  <div class="wrap how-part solo-head"><div class="sec-head">
    <h2>{T('Phone Remote')}</h2>
    <p class="lede">{T('Shift and control your ride from a phone or tablet on the same Wi-Fi. No app to install, and no internet needed.')}</p>
  </div></div>
  <!-- Built like the solo scene: steps left, diagram right (src/scripts/motion.ts). The phone and
       the computer talk over the home network only, so the link is green, like the device's own. -->
  <div class="scene-pin" id="remote-pin">
    <div class="wrap scene" id="remote-scene">
      <ol class="steps timeline" id="remote-steps">
        <li class="c-off"><h3 class="h3">{T('Turn It On')}</h3><p>{T('In ORQWA, open Devices and switch on the remote. A QR code appears on the screen.')}</p></li>
        <li class="c-off"><h3 class="h3">{T('Scan the Code')}</h3><p>{T('Make sure your phone or tablet is on the same Wi-Fi as the computer, then scan the code with its camera. The remote opens in the browser.')}</p></li>
        <li class="c-off"><h3 class="h3">{T('Ride')}</h3><p>{T('Shift gears, pause or change the camera from your phone. It talks to the computer over your Wi-Fi, so no internet connection is needed.')}</p></li>
        <li class="c-off"><h3 class="h3">{T('Who Can Use It')}</h3><p>{T('The remote only works on phones that have scanned the code. To stop a phone from using it, make a new code in ORQWA.')}</p></li>
